    {
      "id": "598519a67cec0a979df70b09ec5ceeac734f88a0",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 594179310,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Note the comment in epan/export_object.h:\n\n         ...\n\n      XXX - we store the entire object in the program's address space,\n      so the *real* maximum object size is size_t; if we were to export\n      objects by going through all of the packets containing data from\n      the object, one packet at a time, and write the object incrementally,\n      we could support objects that don't fit into the address space. */\n\nIn practice, what's pointed to by the `content` argument to `write_file_binary_mode()` can never be larger than the maximum value of a `size_t`, as nothing in the process's address space can be larger than that.  (The address space *as a whole* can't be larger than that on all the platforms on which we run; on ILP32 platforms, `size_t` is a 32-bit unsigned value, and on LP64 (64-bit UN\\*Xes) and LLP64 (64-bit Windows) `size_t` is a 64-bit unsigned value.)\n\nThe `payload_len` member of a `export_object_entry_t` structure presumably is a `gint64` because somewhere in the process a `gint64` value is assigned to it.",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1b7c243a9b1d6587a9a9067e5d83aba1e87212df7c4eeae3690f791ecbe4675a?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/guyharris"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-06-07T09:45:35.478Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-06-07T09:45:35.478Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 103014352,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
